Let's break down each new property:

- `filter: drop-shadow(15px 15px 15px gray) brightness(0.9);` - This applies a drop shadow (similar to what you already have) but also reduces the brightness of the element by 10%. This helps create a sense of depth and makes the circle appear less intense.
- `transform-style: preserve-3d;` - This tells the browser to treat this element as a 3D object instead of flattened on the screen.
- `transform: translateZ(5px);` - This moves the element slightly forward along the Z axis (perpendicular to the screen). You may need to adjust this value to suit your design needs.

These changes should give your circles a more 3D appearance! Let me know if you have any further questions or concerns.

