best_response:
To push the `mnpStatus` received from the API into the corresponding registration object in your state, you can modify your `checkMNPStatusAPI` function as follows:

 ```javascript
 checkMNPStatusAPI(phoneNo, index) {
   console.log("mnpphoneno: ", phoneNo);

   var headers = new Headers();
   headers.append("Authorization", "Bearer " + user.getAccessToken());

   fetch(api.checkPortInStatus(user.getProductCode(), phoneNo), {
     headers: headers,
     method: 'GET'
   })
     .then(r => r.json())
     .then(rjson => {
       const { status } = rjson;

       // update state with new mnpStatus
       const updatedRegistrations = [...this.state.registrations];
       updatedRegistrations[index].mnpStatus = status;
       this.setState({ registrations: updatedRegistrations });
     })
     .catch(error => {
       console.log("Error: ", error);
     });
 }
 ```

 In this modified version, we first save the current state of `registrations` in a new array called `updatedRegistrations`. We then access the specific registration object at the given `index`, update its `mnpStatus` property with the value received from the API, and replace the entire `registrations` state with the updated array.

 Note that we use the spread operator (`...`) to create a shallow copy of the current state, which ensures that the `registrations` state remains unchanged while we update only the relevant object within it.

Here's a PowerShell script that recursively checks folders for ACLs with references to SIDs found only in the SIDHistory of users and groups in the domain:

```powershell
# Set up variables
$domain = (Get-ADDomain).Name
$rootFolderPath = "C:\MyFolder"
$aclFilter = { $_.IdentityReference -match '^S-(?::\d{4})(?::[A-Z0-9]{2}-[A-Z0-9]{2})*(?::[A-Z0-9]{2})(?::[A-Z][A-Z0-9]{7})-[0-9A-F]{8}-[0-9A-F]{4}-[1B][0-9A-F]{12}$' }

# Function to check whether an ACL entry matches the filter
function CheckACLEntry($entry) {
    $sid = [Security.Principal.NTAccount]$entry.IdentityReference
    $sidHistory = (Get-ADUser $sid.SamAccountName).sidHistory
    $sidMatches = $false

    foreach ($histSid in $sidHistory) {
        if ($histSid -eq $entry.IdentityReference) {
            $sidMatches = $true
            break
        }
    }

    return !$sidMatches
}

# Recursive function to check folder ACLs
function CheckFolderACLs($folderPath) {
    $acl = Get-Acl $folderPath

    # Filter out entries that don't match the filter
    $filteredAcl = $acl | Where-Object {$aclFilter -as [scriptblock] $_}

    # Check each filtered entry
    foreach ($entry in $filteredAcl.Access) {
        if (CheckACLEntry $entry) {
            Write-Host "ACL entry with SID '$($entry.IdentityReference)' found in folder '$folderPath'"
        }
    }

    # Recurse into subfolders
    Get-ChildItem $folderPath -Recurse -Directory | ForEach-Object { CheckFolderACLs $_.FullName }
}
